\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and February to March came in under 90% of normal in 32 of them. In 2025 that same pair ran 203% of normal on the middle, while September to October, the wettest pair, ran 71%. So far in 2026, March to April is at 226% on the middle. On grid 31081 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 47.6, an estimate from NOAA rain and not RMA&rsquo;s index.</p>"}
